<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>When you register, request booking assistance, enquire about becoming a partner, or subscribe to updates, we collect the details you provide — typically your name, email, phone number, school or organisation, role and designation. Campaign referral information may also accompany your enquiry.</p>
<h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<p>We use this information to process your registration and enquiries, respond to partnership and booking-assistance requests, send you Summit information and event updates, and improve the Summit experience.</p>
<h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>TezTicket is the planned ticketing partner. Ticketing providers have their own privacy policies governing the information you give them directly. The Summit website uses Google Tag Manager, Meta Pixel and Microsoft Clarity for campaign measurement and website analytics. These services may collect information about your browser, device and interactions with the website, including through cookies or similar technologies. You can manage cookies through your browser settings.</p>
<h2>4. Data Security</h2>
<p>We implement reasonable security measures to protect your information. However, no method of transmission over the internet is completely secure.</p>
<h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
<p>You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information. Contact us at <a href="mailto:summit@theschoolsofindia.org">summit@theschoolsofindia.org</a> to exercise these rights.</p>
<h2>6. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be posted on this page.</p>
<h2>7. Contact</h2>
<p>For privacy questions about the Summit, contact <a href="mailto:summit@theschoolsofindia.org">summit@theschoolsofindia.org</a>.</p>
